# HTML BASIC THEORY NOTES

## 1. Introduction to HTML
HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. It is the standard markup language used to create and structure web pages. HTML describes the structure of a webpage using elements and tags.

## 2. Basic Structure of HTML
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My Webpage</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to HTML</h1>
    <p>This is my first webpage.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

## 3. HTML Tags
HTML tags are keywords enclosed in angle brackets that define elements on a webpage.

Examples:
- `<html>` – Defines the HTML document.
- `<head>` – Contains metadata.
- `<title>` – Defines the webpage title.
- `<body>` – Contains visible webpage content.
- `<p>` – Defines a paragraph.
- `<h1>` – Defines a main heading.

## 4. HTML Headings
HTML provides six levels of headings, from `<h1>` to `<h6>`. The `<h1>` tag represents the highest-level heading, while `<h6>` represents the lowest-level heading.

Example:
```html
<h1>Main Heading</h1>
<h2>Subheading</h2>
<h3>Third-Level Heading</h3>
```

## 5. HTML Paragraphs
The `<p>` tag is used to display paragraphs of text on a webpage.

Example:
```html
<p>HTML is used to create web pages.</p>
```

## 6. HTML Text Formatting
HTML provides tags to format text.

- `<b>` – Displays bold text.
- `<strong>` – Indicates important text.
- `<i>` – Displays italic text
